<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">11 December in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 11 December, from 1282 to 1941.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/llywelyn-ap-gruffudd" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/llywelyn-ap-gruffudd.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1282">1282 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">744 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Llywelyn ap Gruffudd, last native Prince of Wales, is killed</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/llywelyn-ap-gruffudd">Llywelyn ap Gruffudd</a> was killed near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cilmeri">Cilmeri</a> during Edward I's conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a>. Wales lost its independence, and in 1301 Edward gave the title <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-of-wales">Prince of Wales</a> to his own son.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1688">1688 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">338 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">James II flees London</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">As William of Orange advanced, James II slipped out of Whitehall and dropped the Great Seal into the Thames. Caught at Faversham, he escaped to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> later that month; Parliament treated his flight as abdication.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1792">1792 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">234 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Louis XVI goes on trial before the National Convention</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The deposed king, now called Louis Capet, appeared before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-convention">National Convention</a> to answer charges of treason. He was convicted and guillotined in January 1793.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1936">1936 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">90 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Edward VIII abdicates to marry Wallis Simpson</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The abdication took legal effect, and that evening Edward broadcast that he could not reign 'without the help and support of the woman I love'. His brother succeeded as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-vi">George VI</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1941">1941 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">85 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Germany and Italy declare war on the United States</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Four days after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attack-on-pearl-harbor">Pearl Harbor</a>, Hitler and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benito-mussolini">Mussolini</a> declared war on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>. The decision brought American power fully into the war in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li></ol>
